1
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,318
{\an8}<i>The winner of</i> I Am Boxer <i>will receive</i>

2
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:19,920
{\an8}<i>a grand prize of 300 million won</i>

3
00:00:19,987 --> 00:00:23,223
{\an8}<i>and a top-of-the-line flagship SUV.</i>

4
00:00:26,627 --> 00:00:30,531
This is the <i>I Am Boxer</i> deathmatch,
and we're down to the final bout.

5
00:00:31,465 --> 00:00:33,100
It's finally the last one.

6
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,236
Now, these two
must've sparked the question,

7
00:00:36,303 --> 00:00:38,505
- "Who'd win if they squared off?"
- Yes.

8
00:00:38,572 --> 00:00:40,207
- Here we go.
- It's a big match.

9
00:00:40,274 --> 00:00:41,675
Here we go, the real deal.

10
00:00:41,742 --> 00:00:43,677
It's a giant versus a giant.

11
00:00:44,244 --> 00:00:47,681
Myung Hyunman from the blue
corner versus Julien Kang from the red.

12
00:00:47,748 --> 00:00:49,783
They're facing off in this deathmatch.

13
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:51,785
Oh!

14
00:00:52,619 --> 00:00:54,354
Unbelievable.

15
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:55,756
Feels like a knockout is coming.

16
00:00:55,822 --> 00:00:57,791
This is the kind of matchup
you only dream about.

17
00:00:57,858 --> 00:00:59,426
And now, we actually get to see it.

18
00:00:59,493 --> 00:01:02,896
I'm sure the viewers have been
waiting for this matchup.

19
00:01:02,963 --> 00:01:05,599
It's the kind of fight you'd pay to watch.
Want to chip in?

20
00:01:06,867 --> 00:01:10,037
All right.
Please get ready for the fight.

21
00:01:11,438 --> 00:01:13,440
<i>He's built for strength.</i>

22
00:01:13,507 --> 00:01:16,243
<i>You don't see
physicality like that around here.</i>

23
00:01:16,810 --> 00:01:18,412
<i>Look at those shoulders.</i>

24
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:20,747
<i>Julien's got a crazy reach.</i>

25
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:22,115
<i>I know.</i>

26
00:01:22,182 --> 00:01:23,750
<i>Look, that's insane.</i>

27
00:01:24,551 --> 00:01:27,254
<i>I'm pretty confident.
I'm just gonna go all the way.</i>

28
00:01:27,321 --> 00:01:28,488
<i>Whatever. I have to.</i>

29
00:01:28,555 --> 00:01:31,625
<i>I thought I'd better
finish him off fast and move on.</i>

30
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:35,262
<i>Captain America versus Human Weapon.</i>

31
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:38,098
Good luck to you both. Give it your all.

32
00:01:38,165 --> 00:01:39,199
All right. Box!

33
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:42,269
{\an8}ROUND 1 OF 2
JULIEN KANG X MYUNG HYUNMAN

34
00:01:45,539 --> 00:01:47,874
{\an8}- Just use the jab a lot!
- The ring looks small.

35
00:01:50,677 --> 00:01:54,348
Hey! Oh!

36
00:01:56,049 --> 00:01:58,118
Every shot looks so damn powerful.

37
00:01:58,185 --> 00:02:00,187
A punch like that could kill you.

38
00:02:00,253 --> 00:02:02,823
Yeah, if that overhand right lands.

39
00:02:03,757 --> 00:02:05,459
If one of those lands, it's over.

40
00:02:05,525 --> 00:02:06,827
They punch like...

41
00:02:06,893 --> 00:02:08,462
I'm shaking just watching this.

42
00:02:08,528 --> 00:02:10,030
One shot could drop them.

43
00:02:11,098 --> 00:02:13,100
Neither of them throws light punches.

44
00:02:17,037 --> 00:02:18,772
This is all about the one big shot.

45
00:02:19,272 --> 00:02:22,309
- Man, his reach is insane.
- Those arms.

46
00:02:22,376 --> 00:02:24,411
He's got knockout power.

47
00:02:25,012 --> 00:02:27,748
Each shot looks so heavy.

48
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:29,950
Just watching heavyweights square off

49
00:02:30,017 --> 00:02:32,285
gives you a thrill because of the tension.

50
00:02:32,352 --> 00:02:34,955
There's a reason
heavyweight fights are most popular.

51
00:02:35,022 --> 00:02:36,056
Those huge swings...

52
00:02:36,123 --> 00:02:37,858
- Oh, nice counter!
- That was close.

53
00:02:38,525 --> 00:02:39,993
This is terrifying.

54
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,528
- Seriously.
- I'm sweating.

55
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:45,232
It's nerve-racking
even without many clean shots.

56
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:47,601
Imagine how tense they must be.

57
00:02:48,268 --> 00:02:50,203
They're being extremely cautious.

58
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:52,506
- Because one clean shot could end it.
- Exactly.

59
00:02:52,572 --> 00:02:55,308
How do you jump in when you know
one shot could knock you out?

60
00:02:58,945 --> 00:03:00,514
That's gonna be tough to get through.

61
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:02,182
His reach makes it hard.

62
00:03:02,249 --> 00:03:04,451
He can't step in
because the reach is too long.

63
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:06,053
He's good at keeping distance.

64
00:03:07,254 --> 00:03:10,691
<i>With heavyweights,
one clean shot, and you're done.</i>

65
00:03:10,757 --> 00:03:13,960
<i>So I was just focused on
controlling the range.</i>

66
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:15,696
<i>When he stepped into my range,</i>

67
00:03:15,762 --> 00:03:19,132
<i>I hit him with a right or a jab.</i>

68
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:22,869
It's tough to close the distance.

69
00:03:22,936 --> 00:03:26,873
This is easier for someone
who's good at controlling the range.

70
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:30,577
Guess it's hard to
close in on Julien, even for Hyunman.

71
00:03:32,245 --> 00:03:34,147
How are his arms so long?

72
00:03:34,948 --> 00:03:36,717
Yeah, like that! Like that.

73
00:03:38,385 --> 00:03:40,587
He's making good use of his long arms.

74
00:03:40,654 --> 00:03:42,022
His physicality is unreal.

75
00:03:42,089 --> 00:03:45,192
- Julien's got freaking long arms.
- Too long.

76
00:03:45,258 --> 00:03:47,360
- Seriously.
- Yeah, you can't find an opening.

77
00:03:47,427 --> 00:03:48,895
He's doing better than I thought.

78
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:52,399
He's using his long reach
to his advantage.

79
00:03:52,466 --> 00:03:53,667
Damn.

80
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,372
Man, it's like a cannon shot.

81
00:04:01,475 --> 00:04:03,643
His punching power is insane.

82
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:05,412
- That's a smart move.
- Push!

83
00:04:05,479 --> 00:04:08,048
- It's a smart move.
- Clinching, huh?

84
00:04:08,115 --> 00:04:09,549
It's a solid plan.

85
00:04:10,817 --> 00:04:13,186
You can feel
how insanely strong they both are.

86
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:15,756
- Their strength is just...
- It's like...

87
00:04:17,524 --> 00:04:19,726
It's hard to fight someone
with that kind of body,

88
00:04:19,793 --> 00:04:21,061
even if he's not a boxer.

89
00:04:24,698 --> 00:04:26,166
They can't step in easily.

90
00:04:27,334 --> 00:04:28,969
Ten seconds!

91
00:04:29,736 --> 00:04:31,671
I'd say whoever closes in first wins.

92
00:04:31,738 --> 00:04:33,874
Their punches are like nuclear bombs.

93
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,308
{\an8}Stop!

94
00:04:35,375 --> 00:04:36,376
{\an8}ROUND 1 IS OVER

95
00:04:36,977 --> 00:04:38,645
Julien's gonna stick to that game plan.

96
00:04:38,712 --> 00:04:39,746
- Yeah, I bet.
- Hmm.

97
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:42,082
Then you never know how it'll end.

98
00:04:42,149 --> 00:04:43,817
He came up with a good plan.

99
00:04:43,884 --> 00:04:45,485
Yeah, so Hyunman?

100
00:04:46,386 --> 00:04:49,456
He should throw a jab
and then go for body shots.

101
00:04:49,523 --> 00:04:51,258
Body shots, and then up to the head.

102
00:04:51,324 --> 00:04:54,661
And if he closes in like that,
Julien should hit and move.

103
00:04:55,228 --> 00:04:59,366
<i>Julien Kang was
keeping his distance with his lead hand.</i>

104
00:04:59,432 --> 00:05:02,102
It threw me off a bit,

105
00:05:02,769 --> 00:05:06,339
and I had to figure out
how to get past it.

106
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:09,810
Let's go, Julien!

107
00:05:12,779 --> 00:05:14,080
Come on, let's go!

108
00:05:14,881 --> 00:05:15,882
Let's do this!

109
00:05:17,017 --> 00:05:18,451
{\an8}- You got this!
- Box!

110
00:05:18,518 --> 00:05:21,788
{\an8}ROUND 2 OF 2
JULIEN KANG X MYUNG HYUNMAN

111
00:05:22,722 --> 00:05:24,624
{\an8}They're being cautious.

112
00:05:38,405 --> 00:05:40,273
Oh, he got caught.

113
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:42,509
Julien Kang's got powerful punches too.

114
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:45,946
Man, that was close.

115
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:47,647
That could've knocked him down.

116
00:05:47,714 --> 00:05:50,483
If one of those lands,
you're done. This is just...

117
00:05:50,550 --> 00:05:54,020
Julien Kang keeps driving
those long shots in.

118
00:05:54,087 --> 00:05:55,922
That makes it one-nothing.

119
00:05:55,989 --> 00:05:58,258
- Yes, go again! Again!
- You got this!

120
00:05:58,859 --> 00:06:00,327
He just switched to southpaw.

121
00:06:00,393 --> 00:06:02,128
That might actually work better for him.

122
00:06:05,565 --> 00:06:07,033
- You got it!
- Go! Get on him!

123
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,302
- That's it!
- Push him off!

124
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:10,470
That's the right move.

125
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:13,139
He needs to switch to southpaw
and crack him with a hook.

126
00:06:14,441 --> 00:06:16,877
<i>I changed my stance
from orthodox to southpaw.</i>

127
00:06:16,943 --> 00:06:21,147
<i>I assumed he hadn't fought
a lot of left-handed fighters.</i>

128
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:24,284
I tried to attack more with my left hand.

129
00:06:24,351 --> 00:06:26,453
Keep your distance! Focus!

130
00:06:42,302 --> 00:06:45,005
Down, down, down! He's down!

131
00:06:52,746 --> 00:06:54,147
Down, down, down.

132
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:57,751
Two!

133
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,320
- Three! Four!
- He's down!

134
00:07:03,189 --> 00:07:04,691
<i>I took a few shots there.</i>

135
00:07:05,191 --> 00:07:06,559
And after that,

136
00:07:06,626 --> 00:07:09,329
I couldn't think about the next step.

137
00:07:09,396 --> 00:07:10,397
Ready?

138
00:07:10,931 --> 00:07:12,899
- Box!
- Lead hand up! One-two!

139
00:07:12,966 --> 00:07:15,068
Stay far away. Stay away from him.

140
00:07:16,736 --> 00:07:18,838
This means a clean shot
really would drop him.

141
00:07:18,905 --> 00:07:21,107
He's clearly not used to taking hits.

142
00:07:21,675 --> 00:07:23,310
He went down from a single shot.

143
00:07:28,748 --> 00:07:30,617
See? A hook like that.

144
00:07:34,721 --> 00:07:37,757
{\an8}JULIEN KANG'S SECOND KNOCKDOWN

145
00:07:39,526 --> 00:07:40,760
He really is strong.

146
00:07:41,728 --> 00:07:43,730
Hyunman's freaking strong, seriously.

147
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:45,131
- Box!
- Ten seconds!

148
00:07:45,198 --> 00:07:48,001
<i>Even if I get KO'd,
it'd still be an honor.</i>

149
00:07:48,068 --> 00:07:50,537
<i>He's a great fighter.
I just wanted to fight to the end.</i>

150
00:07:51,271 --> 00:07:52,539
- Ten seconds!
- This is it!

151
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:55,408
Julien, 10 seconds! 10 seconds!

152
00:07:57,043 --> 00:07:58,645
- Stop!
- All right.

153
00:07:59,412 --> 00:08:00,413
Stop!

154
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,715
- All right.
- All right.

155
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:06,753
{\an8}MATCH OVER

156
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,154
- All right.
- All right.

157
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:10,890
He did the best he could.

158
00:08:10,957 --> 00:08:12,292
- Yeah.
- He put up a good fight.

159
00:08:12,359 --> 00:08:14,027
He had the right game plan.

160
00:08:14,928 --> 00:08:17,030
Julien made it to the end
because he's Julien.

161
00:08:17,097 --> 00:08:19,199
Anyone else
would've been done way earlier.

162
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,869
We'll announce the judges' decision now.

163
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:26,406
By unanimous decision
from both judges,

164
00:08:26,473 --> 00:08:28,942
the survivor of this deathmatch is...

165
00:08:29,776 --> 00:08:31,711
Myung Hyunman.

166
00:08:31,778 --> 00:08:34,414
{\an8}BLUE CORNER
MYUNG HYUNMAN SURVIVES

167
00:08:34,481 --> 00:08:36,983
The truth is, this was

168
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:40,186
the first real fight of my life.

169
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:44,024
I was unlucky to get matched...

170
00:08:44,090 --> 00:08:46,326
...with someone like Hyunman

171
00:08:46,393 --> 00:08:48,328
for my first fight, and that's too bad.

172
00:08:48,395 --> 00:08:50,764
But it was a great learning experience.

173
00:08:50,830 --> 00:08:53,199
Myung Hyunman was amazing today,

174
00:08:53,266 --> 00:08:55,635
so I just have to admit defeat.

175
00:08:57,003 --> 00:08:58,605
Thank you for a great fight.

176
00:08:58,671 --> 00:09:00,740
Well done, both of you.
Thank you so much.

177
00:09:00,807 --> 00:09:01,808
Well done.

178
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,949
<i>I never saw that coming.</i>

179
00:09:10,683 --> 00:09:13,053
<i>This show always
goes beyond my imagination.</i>

180
00:09:13,119 --> 00:09:14,521
<i>Wow, this is insane.</i>

181
00:09:15,155 --> 00:09:18,291
<i>Boxing in an arena
like that? I never even imagined it.</i>

182
00:09:18,358 --> 00:09:21,461
<i>Round 3 of</i> I Am Boxer.

183
00:09:21,528 --> 00:09:22,896
<i>The Three Rings.</i>

184
00:09:24,531 --> 00:09:26,666
- <i>Ready.</i>
- <i>Box!</i>

185
00:09:28,535 --> 00:09:30,170
The <i>I Am Boxer</i> deathmatch.

186
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:32,472
All matches have now come to an end.

187
00:09:32,539 --> 00:09:35,308
The six new survivors are...

188
00:09:35,375 --> 00:09:36,776
{\an8}Cho Hyunjae,

189
00:09:37,377 --> 00:09:38,411
{\an8}Kim Taesun,

190
00:09:38,478 --> 00:09:39,612
{\an8}Yuk Junseo,

191
00:09:39,679 --> 00:09:40,847
{\an8}Lee Chaehyun,

192
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,115
{\an8}Kwon Ohgon,

193
00:09:42,182 --> 00:09:43,616
{\an8}and Myung Hyunman.

194
00:09:43,683 --> 00:09:45,085
Congratulations to you all.

195
00:09:49,689 --> 00:09:51,758
<i>That's another cool way to survive.</i>

196
00:09:51,825 --> 00:09:53,560
<i>It's not over till it's over.</i>

197
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:57,797
Well, I thought I bought myself
a little more time.

198
00:09:57,864 --> 00:10:00,066
Next time,
I hope to make it through in one go.

199
00:10:00,867 --> 00:10:02,836
I'll work hard and make that happen.

200
00:10:02,902 --> 00:10:05,972
What I thought was my last chance
didn't end up being my last,

201
00:10:06,039 --> 00:10:08,007
and I'm really grateful about that.

202
00:10:12,345 --> 00:10:13,346
Wow.

203
00:10:14,347 --> 00:10:15,515
Hey.

204
00:10:18,251 --> 00:10:20,420
- Something feels different.
- Right?

205
00:10:20,487 --> 00:10:22,455
Everyone's energy
feels different from last time.

206
00:10:23,857 --> 00:10:25,658
Last time, we were more...

207
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:27,560
There are definitely
a lot fewer people now.

208
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,095
- It's quiet.
- Yeah.

209
00:10:29,162 --> 00:10:31,865
This is everyone?
There really are a lot fewer of us.

210
00:10:31,931 --> 00:10:33,867
- It used to be packed.
- We've really thinned out.

211
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:37,470
I have to win and get
some screen time this round.

212
00:10:37,537 --> 00:10:39,005
I wonder what we're doing today.

213
00:10:39,072 --> 00:10:40,373
Something fun, I hope.

214
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,208
It's probably another game, right?

215
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:44,978
It might be another team round

216
00:10:45,545 --> 00:10:48,314
or just straight-up boxing from here.

217
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:51,751
We have to do another team round.

218
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:53,953
I mean...

219
00:10:57,257 --> 00:10:58,791
- Hi, guys!
- Hello.

220
00:10:58,858 --> 00:11:00,193
- Hello.
- Hi.

221
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:02,228
- Hello.
- They've just been relaxing.

222
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:04,731
- There are a lot fewer people now.
- Yeah.

223
00:11:04,797 --> 00:11:06,766
- We're down a lot of people.
- Clearly.

224
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,968
Way fewer people. Hi, guys.

225
00:11:09,602 --> 00:11:11,171
- Well, now it feels...
- Hi, there.

226
00:11:11,237 --> 00:11:13,606
We've gotten familiar
with each other now,

227
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:16,109
and I feel closer to them.

228
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:20,079
We now have a
pretty good sense of who everyone is.

229
00:11:20,146 --> 00:11:22,982
All right. Before we start Round 3,

230
00:11:23,049 --> 00:11:25,552
we have an announcement.

231
00:11:25,618 --> 00:11:29,522
Yang Sellchan had to leave the show
for personal reasons.

232
00:11:29,589 --> 00:11:33,459
- So we needed a replacement.
- Sellchan?

233
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:35,895
Here's our new survivor.

234
00:11:35,962 --> 00:11:38,665
Here's our new survivor.

235
00:11:38,731 --> 00:11:40,667
- Who could it be?
- Who is it?

236
00:11:40,733 --> 00:11:42,235
Open sesame.

237
00:11:44,504 --> 00:11:46,105
I have a funny feeling.

238
00:11:46,773 --> 00:11:48,575
- Minuk?
- Come on, no way.

239
00:11:48,641 --> 00:11:50,643
- Well, it feels like...
- No way.

240
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:51,911
No, it can't be.

241
00:11:51,978 --> 00:11:54,247
I'm getting PTSD just thinking about it.

242
00:11:54,314 --> 00:11:55,481
No way.

243
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,217
Could it be Julien Kang?

244
00:11:57,283 --> 00:11:59,819
All right, let's bring in
the new survivor.

245
00:12:03,756 --> 00:12:05,358
Well, who could it be?

246
00:12:05,425 --> 00:12:07,026
This is exciting.

247
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:15,034
{\an8}I knew it.

248
00:12:15,101 --> 00:12:16,436
{\an8}I knew it.

249
00:12:16,502 --> 00:12:17,537
{\an8}NEW SURVIVOR, KIM MINUK

250
00:12:21,908 --> 00:12:23,576
I'm getting PTSD.

