There's no tag team in boxing.

1241
00:57:00,017 --> 00:57:01,184
- No.
- Nothing like that.

1242
00:57:01,251 --> 00:57:02,452
- I mean...
- This is new.

1243
00:57:02,519 --> 00:57:04,021
...we've never seen anything like this.

1244
00:57:04,087 --> 00:57:07,090
- No cross-weight fights or team events.
- Right.

1245
00:57:07,691 --> 00:57:09,226
They never fight as a team.

1246
00:57:09,660 --> 00:57:11,228
This is so original.

1247
00:57:11,295 --> 00:57:14,364
<i>When your name is called,</i>

1248
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:16,700
<i>please step into the ring.</i>

1249
00:57:17,868 --> 00:57:19,002
Who's up first?

1250
00:57:19,069 --> 00:57:20,237
Who's it gonna be?

1251
00:57:20,304 --> 00:57:21,338
Who is it?

1252
00:57:21,405 --> 00:57:22,606
Who?

1253
00:57:24,207 --> 00:57:25,676
Here we go.

1254
00:57:25,742 --> 00:57:26,910
Who's up first?

1255
00:57:26,977 --> 00:57:27,978
Who's going first?

1256
00:57:30,814 --> 00:57:31,949
Let's have some fun.

1257
00:57:32,449 --> 00:57:33,650
Well, I'm a little nervous.

1258
00:57:34,518 --> 00:57:35,719
<i>Red corner.</i>

1259
00:57:37,587 --> 00:57:39,957
<i>Lee Chaehyun, Cho Hyunjae.</i>

1260
00:57:41,191 --> 00:57:43,093
- All right, let's go!
- Let's go!

1261
00:57:43,160 --> 00:57:44,494
All right!

1262
00:57:44,561 --> 00:57:46,029
They're one of the tough ones.

1263
00:57:46,096 --> 00:57:47,364
Both KAFAC boxers.

1264
00:57:48,098 --> 00:57:50,334
They're the pride of the Korean army.

1265
00:57:50,400 --> 00:57:53,136
They're both from
the Korea Armed Forces Athletic Corps.

1266
00:57:54,371 --> 00:57:58,909
I wanted to team up
with Lee Chaehyun from the KAFAC.

1267
00:57:58,976 --> 00:58:00,811
I picked Cho Hyunjae straightaway.

1268
00:58:00,877 --> 00:58:03,046
KAFAC boxers pairing up? That's not fair.

1269
00:58:04,181 --> 00:58:05,182
<i>Blue corner.</i>

1270
00:58:05,649 --> 00:58:08,218
<i>Park Sungwoon, Jin Youmin.</i>

1271
00:58:08,719 --> 00:58:10,620
- Oh no!
- Let's go!

1272
00:58:10,687 --> 00:58:12,489
Hey, you scared me.

1273
00:58:12,556 --> 00:58:14,091
Love that energy!

1274
00:58:14,992 --> 00:58:17,060
Wow, that's some real grit.

1275
00:58:17,894 --> 00:58:19,229
They need to use their size.

1276
00:58:19,296 --> 00:58:21,832
Right, they need to use
their weight advantage.

1277
00:58:22,299 --> 00:58:27,204
<i>Hyunjae and Chaehyun were the ones
I thought would be the toughest to beat,</i>

1278
00:58:27,270 --> 00:58:29,039
<i>so I was a bit on edge.</i>

1279
00:58:29,106 --> 00:58:31,975
But I'm bigger than both of them,

1280
00:58:32,042 --> 00:58:33,610
so I figured I'd just knock them out.

1281
00:58:34,177 --> 00:58:36,580
I'm sure a lot of you
are excited about this match.

1282
00:58:36,646 --> 00:58:39,316
Before we start,
let's hear the fighters' thoughts.

1283
00:58:39,383 --> 00:58:41,885
I'll show you I can fight well

1284
00:58:41,952 --> 00:58:43,553
no matter what kind of ring I'm in.

1285
00:58:43,620 --> 00:58:45,055
Spoken like a true soldier.

1286
00:58:45,122 --> 00:58:46,823
He kept it polite.

1287
00:58:48,125 --> 00:58:50,827
I heard they're from
the Korea Armed Forces Athletic Corps.

1288
00:58:51,328 --> 00:58:53,697
I'll knock them out
and get them discharged.

1289
00:58:54,464 --> 00:58:55,799
...and get them discharged.

1290
00:58:59,302 --> 00:59:00,737
- Good one.
- He got them.

1291
00:59:05,809 --> 00:59:06,843
Oh, boy.

1292
00:59:06,910 --> 00:59:08,945
That's bold.

1293
00:59:09,746 --> 00:59:11,982
That's some serious determination.

1294
00:59:13,316 --> 00:59:14,985
Wow, hey.

1295
00:59:15,986 --> 00:59:17,487
Well, he really is a lot bigger.

1296
00:59:17,554 --> 00:59:18,655
- He is.
- Yeah.

1297
00:59:19,289 --> 00:59:20,957
It's not just his weight.

1298
00:59:21,024 --> 00:59:23,126
- His reach too. He's much taller.
- That's right.

1299
00:59:23,627 --> 00:59:27,431
Chaehyun and Hyunjae are both out-boxers

1300
00:59:27,497 --> 00:59:29,099
who rely on speed.

1301
00:59:29,166 --> 00:59:32,769
I know they're good, but can they
overcome the weight difference?

1302
00:59:32,836 --> 00:59:34,271
- Right.
- And the ring.

1303
00:59:35,505 --> 00:59:38,875
On paper, Red should win, but...

1304
00:59:39,743 --> 00:59:41,912
I know. It's not gonna be easy.

1305
00:59:43,080 --> 00:59:46,383
I wonder who's gonna go first
between those two.

1306
00:59:47,017 --> 00:59:48,118
Probably the heavyweight.

1307
00:59:48,185 --> 00:59:50,854
Is the heavyweight gonna come out first
and clean them out?

1308
00:59:50,921 --> 00:59:53,323
<i>The match will begin now.</i>

1309
00:59:53,990 --> 00:59:56,493
<i>Fighters going first,</i>

1310
00:59:57,027 --> 00:59:58,028
<i>step into the ring.</i>

1311
00:59:58,962 --> 01:00:01,064
I think it's Park Sungwoon. I knew it.

1312
01:00:01,798 --> 01:00:02,899
{\an8}PARK SUNGWOON GOES FIRST

1313
01:00:02,966 --> 01:00:05,001
{\an8}- Go, Toongsoon!
- All right!

1314
01:00:06,036 --> 01:00:07,704
{\an8}Lee Chaehyun's going first.

1315
01:00:07,771 --> 01:00:08,905
{\an8}Let's go, Chaehyun!

1316
01:00:08,972 --> 01:00:10,674
{\an8}- This is gonna be fun.
- Well, this is...

1317
01:00:10,740 --> 01:00:13,577
I think it's a nice way
to kick it off, for both of them.

1318
01:00:13,643 --> 01:00:14,644
- You got this!
- Good luck!

1319
01:00:14,711 --> 01:00:16,279
You can see the size difference.

1320
01:00:16,346 --> 01:00:17,347
Who's gonna win?

1321
01:00:18,482 --> 01:00:20,984
<i>The match will begin now.</i>

1322
01:00:24,154 --> 01:00:25,188
Box!

1323
01:00:25,755 --> 01:00:27,090
{\an8}- Don't go in first.
- All right!

1324
01:00:27,157 --> 01:00:28,325
{\an8}- Go!
- Loosen up.

1325
01:00:28,391 --> 01:00:30,193
{\an8}- Okay, good.
- Just do what you always do.

1326
01:00:31,194 --> 01:00:32,596
{\an8}All right, nice!

1327
01:00:32,662 --> 01:00:34,664
Tuck your chin and loosen up!
Hey, nice jab!

1328
01:00:34,731 --> 01:00:36,032
Chaehyun, shoot it up!

1329
01:00:36,099 --> 01:00:37,100
That's it.

1330
01:00:37,167 --> 01:00:38,301
All right, good.

1331
01:00:38,368 --> 01:00:39,903
See? You get pushed back like that.

1332
01:00:39,970 --> 01:00:41,404
He's faster than I thought.

1333
01:00:41,471 --> 01:00:42,472
No clinching.

1334
01:00:42,539 --> 01:00:44,407
Getting pressed down like that drains you.

1335
01:00:44,474 --> 01:00:45,942
Shoot it up! Throw it upward!

1336
01:00:46,676 --> 01:00:48,111
That's it! Doing great!

1337
01:00:49,379 --> 01:00:50,714
He's good.

1338
01:00:50,780 --> 01:00:51,982
There you go!

1339
01:00:52,048 --> 01:00:53,183
Cover up, all right?

1340
01:00:53,250 --> 01:00:56,119
- Park Sungwoon can take hits.
- That's a real fighter right there.

1341
01:00:56,186 --> 01:00:57,287
All right, good.

1342
01:00:57,354 --> 01:00:59,389
- But we'll have to see if he can last.
- Right.

1343
01:01:06,763 --> 01:01:08,565
You got him!

1344
01:01:10,367 --> 01:01:11,434
- Wait, what?
- What?

1345
01:01:11,501 --> 01:01:12,536
What?

1346
01:01:12,602 --> 01:01:14,037
Wow, that looked heavy.

1347
01:01:14,104 --> 01:01:16,106
- Sungwoon hasn't taken any shots.
- Right.

1348
01:01:16,673 --> 01:01:19,009
Chaehyun's taken quite a few.

1349
01:01:19,075 --> 01:01:20,210
This is gonna be tough.

1350
01:01:21,044 --> 01:01:23,079
Chaehyun, loosen up a little.

1351
01:01:23,146 --> 01:01:24,147
Chaehyun, stay calm!

1352
01:01:24,915 --> 01:01:26,183
Stay calm!

1353
01:01:26,249 --> 01:01:29,319
In a square ring, I can use my speed

1354
01:01:29,386 --> 01:01:31,488
and control the fight.

1355
01:01:31,555 --> 01:01:34,324
<i>But in that ring,
he kept pressing with power,</i>

1356
01:01:34,391 --> 01:01:35,659
and it really threw me off.

1357
01:01:35,725 --> 01:01:37,661
Go to the body and throw some feints.

1358
01:01:37,727 --> 01:01:38,862
Throw it upward!

1359
01:01:38,929 --> 01:01:40,931
What was that?

1360
01:01:43,533 --> 01:01:45,735
You're doing great. Work the jab!

1361
01:01:45,802 --> 01:01:48,238
Feints! That's it! Keep going!

1362
01:01:48,305 --> 01:01:49,439
Yes, that's it!

1363
01:01:49,506 --> 01:01:51,107
- There you go!
- Hey, shoot it up!

1364
01:01:51,508 --> 01:01:53,443
The shots are not doing anything to him.

1365
01:01:53,510 --> 01:01:55,278
Now, up! Throw a hook!

1366
01:01:55,345 --> 01:01:57,314
- That's it!
- Keep going like that!

1367
01:01:58,014 --> 01:01:59,082
Awesome!

1368
01:02:00,283 --> 01:02:01,785
- Extend it!
- "Bring it on."

1369
01:02:01,851 --> 01:02:05,589
He might think
those shots are ineffective,

1370
01:02:05,655 --> 01:02:07,357
but they wear you out

1371
01:02:07,991 --> 01:02:09,226
if you keep taking them.

1372
01:02:10,760 --> 01:02:12,495
- Keep it coming!
- No turning.

1373
01:02:15,432 --> 01:02:16,433
Keep it coming!

1374
01:02:20,036 --> 01:02:21,404
Nice counter.

1375
01:02:21,471 --> 01:02:22,639
Slip and rip!

1376
01:02:22,706 --> 01:02:23,974
That was a slip and uppercut.

1377
01:02:24,507 --> 01:02:26,009
- Wow.
- Just when he stepped in...

1378
01:02:26,076 --> 01:02:27,210
Slip and uppercut.

1379
01:02:28,345 --> 01:02:31,081
It didn't seem like the right time,
but he was waiting for it.

1380
01:02:31,147 --> 01:02:32,415
That's why he kept provoking.

1381
01:02:32,482 --> 01:02:33,750
"Come at me."

1382
01:02:35,418 --> 01:02:36,486
It's okay, it's okay!

1383
01:02:38,455 --> 01:02:40,657
Stay calm, Chaehyun! Stay calm!

1384
01:02:40,724 --> 01:02:42,158
Hey, you're strong!

1385
01:02:42,225 --> 01:02:43,393
You're doing great!

1386
01:02:43,460 --> 01:02:44,461
Wanna switch?

1387
01:02:44,961 --> 01:02:45,962
Keep going!

1388
01:02:48,498 --> 01:02:49,766
- Nice one!
- Great.

1389
01:02:49,833 --> 01:02:51,701
Toongsoon, go to the body first!

1390
01:02:51,768 --> 01:02:53,903
Wait, Park Sungwoon's looking a bit tired.

1391
01:02:53,970 --> 01:02:55,205
- Yeah.
- He's...

1392
01:02:55,272 --> 01:02:57,007
His punches are starting to lose steam.

1393
01:02:57,641 --> 01:02:58,808
He's getting tired now.

1394
01:02:58,875 --> 01:03:01,144
He's starting to breathe heavy.

1395
01:03:01,845 --> 01:03:03,113
Toongsoon, keep moving!

1396
01:03:03,179 --> 01:03:05,615
- Chaehyun, quick shots and get out! Yes!
- All right!

1397
01:03:05,682 --> 01:03:07,017
Uppercut!

1398
01:03:07,083 --> 01:03:08,618
- Nice one.
- Swap!

1399
01:03:10,754 --> 01:03:12,155
{\an8}Hyunjae, you need to move quick!

1400
01:03:13,923 --> 01:03:15,859
- You want to switch?
- He should save his energy.

1401
01:03:15,925 --> 01:03:17,627
{\an8}It's better to switch.

1402
01:03:17,694 --> 01:03:18,695
{\an8}Save your strength.

1403
01:03:19,229 --> 01:03:21,097
{\an8}Jin Youmin's up.

1404
01:03:21,164 --> 01:03:23,166
Let's see if he can keep up
with Cho's speed.

1405
01:03:23,700 --> 01:03:25,568
Hey, he's gonna be even faster.

1406
01:03:26,536 --> 01:03:28,071
- One minute left!
- Let's go!

1407
01:03:28,538 --> 01:03:29,939
{\an8}- Box!
- A pro versus an amateur.

1408
01:03:30,407 --> 01:03:31,908
{\an8}They're fighting for their pride.

1409
01:03:31,975 --> 01:03:33,810
{\an8}ROUND 1 OF 3
CHO HYUNJAE X JIN YOUMIN

1410
01:03:35,445 --> 01:03:36,446
{\an8}Whoa, man.

1411
01:03:36,513 --> 01:03:38,248
- Strong opening.
- He's crazy strong.

1412
01:03:38,315 --> 01:03:39,549
Wow, that grit.

1413
01:03:40,717 --> 01:03:41,718
Box!

1414
01:03:41,785 --> 01:03:43,953
Yes! That's it!

1415
01:03:44,020 --> 01:03:45,722
That looked heavy.

1416
01:03:45,789 --> 01:03:48,191
A pro would definitely have
the upper hand in this ring.

1417
01:03:48,258 --> 01:03:49,693
Yeah, there's no where to run.

1418
01:03:50,160 --> 01:03:51,995
The ring really changes the game.

1419
01:03:52,529 --> 01:03:55,632
<i>It was tougher than I thought.
The ring was different,</i>

1420
01:03:55,699 --> 01:03:57,634
<i>and he kept coming in with his head down.</i>

1421
01:03:57,701 --> 01:03:59,736
<i>It was a bit frustrating.</i>

1422
01:04:00,303 --> 01:04:02,605
<i>Still, I was confident in my speed,</i>

1423
01:04:02,672 --> 01:04:05,175
so I figured
I'd just throw a lot and throw fast.

1424
01:04:06,976 --> 01:04:08,278
- Nice!
- Good going!

1425
01:04:08,345 --> 01:04:09,646
Wow, they're fast.

1426
01:04:09,713 --> 01:04:11,081
Smart moves!

1427
01:04:11,147 --> 01:04:12,248
Hyunjae's so good.

1428
01:04:12,682 --> 01:04:13,817
Doing great, Hyunjae!

1429
01:04:14,718 --> 01:04:16,553
Jin Youmin keeps...

1430
01:04:16,619 --> 01:04:18,421
He keeps going in with his head down.

1431
01:04:18,488 --> 01:04:20,724
He's aiming too low, isn't he?

1432
01:04:20,790 --> 01:04:22,525
He doesn't have to do that.

1433
01:04:22,592 --> 01:04:23,660
Stay calm!

1434
01:04:23,727 --> 01:04:24,928
Ten seconds!

1435
01:04:24,994 --> 01:04:26,229
He doesn't have to do that.

1436
01:04:26,296 --> 01:04:28,331
- No, he doesn't.
- Watch it.

1437
01:04:28,398 --> 01:04:30,266
He's hitting a lot of arms
instead of the head.

1438
01:04:30,900 --> 01:04:32,068
Cho's good at clinching.

1439
01:04:32,135 --> 01:04:33,303
Stop!

1440
01:04:33,370 --> 01:04:34,671
Good, good, good.

1441
01:04:34,738 --> 01:04:35,905
Well done.

1442
01:04:35,972 --> 01:04:37,240
- That was good.
- Yeah.

1443
01:04:37,307 --> 01:04:41,177
Oh. It's not that
Jin Youmin lacks technique,

1444
01:04:41,745 --> 01:04:43,780
- so why go in blind like that?
- He's fired up today.

1445
01:04:43,847 --> 01:04:46,916
I think that's his plan today,
to keep pressuring.

1446
01:04:46,983 --> 01:04:48,385
But with his head down like this,

1447
01:04:48,885 --> 01:04:51,154
his aim naturally drops.

1448
01:04:51,221 --> 01:04:53,656
Toongsoon is so much better
than I expected, by the way.

1449
01:04:54,524 --> 01:04:56,626
Park Sungwoon was like...

1450
01:04:56,693 --> 01:04:57,827
He's got a heavy punch.

1451
01:04:58,328 --> 01:05:00,563
Toongsoon, take your time in there.

1452
01:05:01,364 --> 01:05:03,133
- He's good.
- You're winning.

1453
01:05:06,236 --> 01:05:08,271
After taking a few shots, I realized

1454
01:05:08,338 --> 01:05:09,839
there's not much to those elite boxers.

1455
01:05:09,906 --> 01:05:10,974
I was ready to fight it out.

1456
01:05:11,474 --> 01:05:13,209
I bet Red's got a lot to think about.

1457
01:05:13,276 --> 01:05:14,277
You need more rest?

1458
01:05:14,677 --> 01:05:16,780
- Are you all recovered now?
- Yeah, I am.

1459
01:05:16,846 --> 01:05:17,981
- I'm not tired.
- All right.

1460
01:05:18,481 --> 01:05:20,183
- It's the weight difference.
- Mmm.

1461
01:05:20,250 --> 01:05:21,384
- I was...
- You should...

1462
01:05:22,018 --> 01:05:23,953
- Get more snap in your punches.
- Faster?

1463
01:05:24,020 --> 01:05:25,021
Get more snap in them.

1464
01:05:25,088 --> 01:05:27,624
- I tried to take him head-on at first.
- It's fine.

1465
01:05:28,191 --> 01:05:29,292
Should I go first?

1466
01:05:29,959 --> 01:05:31,394
What if the big one comes out?

1467
01:05:31,461 --> 01:05:32,929
I'll try to get him with quick shots.

1468
01:05:32,996 --> 01:05:34,764
If it doesn't work, you can tag in.

1469
01:05:34,831 --> 01:05:35,899
We can switch then.

1470
01:05:38,101 --> 01:05:40,270
<i>Fighters, step into the ring.</i>

1471
01:05:40,336 --> 01:05:42,105
Come on, let's go!

1472
01:05:42,172 --> 01:05:43,640
Who's up... Oh, damn.

1473
01:05:43,706 --> 01:05:44,808
Damn.

1474
01:05:45,308 --> 01:05:46,876
What? You sure?

1475
01:05:48,077 --> 01:05:49,446
Oh.

1476
01:05:49,512 --> 01:05:52,048
{\an8}RED CORNER'S FIRST FIGHTER IN
CHO HYUNJAE 118 CM/98 KG

1477
01:05:52,115 --> 01:05:54,551
{\an8}Cho Hyunjae versus Park Sungwoon.

1478
01:05:54,951 --> 01:05:57,120
- He looks like a giant next to him.
- Yeah.

1479
01:05:57,187 --> 01:05:58,388
I can't wait to see this.

1480
01:05:58,455 --> 01:06:00,423
There's a serious weight difference.

1481
01:06:00,490 --> 01:06:02,892
They're 34 kg apart.

1482
01:06:02,959 --> 01:06:04,828
{\an8}- Oh!
- Come on, let's go!

1483
01:06:05,295 --> 01:06:07,530
<i>A fly's buzzing in my face.
Let me kill it.</i>

1484
01:06:08,331 --> 01:06:11,835
<i>I'll prove to you
that boxing isn't about size.</i>

1485
01:06:14,137 --> 01:06:15,138
Box!

1486
01:06:15,205 --> 01:06:17,607
{\an8}ROUND 2 OF 3
CHO HYUNJAE X PARK SUNGWOON

1487
01:06:17,674 --> 01:06:19,609
{\an8}- Box!
- Move after you hit!

1488
01:06:22,378 --> 01:06:23,780
{\an8}- Great!
- Yeah!

1489
